      "writtenOn": "2023-07-20T01:04:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the review. We would like to follow the guideline to SET and VERIFY as followed.\n\nFor the setting part, the user of this api would be within VMM like Crosvm[1], and zero-filled of this padding would be default behavior for now[2].\n\nFor the verifying part, we\u0027re going to check the zeros somehow similar to the  following pseudo code which would be patched in `gzvm_irqfd.c` when the ioctl is triggered[3].\n\n```\nint gzvm_irqfd(struct gzvm *gzvm, struct gzvm_irqfd *args)\n{\n    ...snip...\n \n    int n \u003d sizeof(args.pad) / sizeof(args.pad[0]);\n    for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c n; i++)\n    {\n        if(args.pad[i])\n            return -EINVAL;\n    }\n \n    ...snip...\n}\n```\n\nreference:\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:external/crosvm/hypervisor/src/geniezone/mod.rs;l\u003d721?q\u003dGZVM_IRQFD\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject\n\n[2] https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/core/default.rs.html#210\n\n[3] https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/2574178/8/drivers/virt/geniezone/gzvm_irqfd.c",
